1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Al-Hakam married Subh of Cordoba, a Basque concubine. She held sway and strong influence over the court. It is said that al-Hakam nicknamed her with the masculine name Ja'far.[6] She bore him two sons, the first is
2 CONC  Abd al-Rahman,[7] who died young, and the second is Hisham II.[8]
