2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Aznar Sánchez de Larraun or Pamplona, born around 858, probably in Larraun, and died around 890, was a member of the nobility of the kingdom of Pamplona in the 9th century. He is the son of Sanche Garcés, himself son of the king o
2 CONC f Pamplona Garcia I and Urrache.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 880, Aznar de Larraun married his cousin, Oneca Fortúnez, daughter of King Fortún Garcés and divorced from the Emir of Cordoba Abd Allah ben Muhammad.
2 CONT
2 CONT From this union are born three children:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Sanche;
2 CONT # Toda (876-958): she married Sanche I, King of Pamplona;
2 CONT # Sancie: she marries Jimeno Garcés de Navarre
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Towards 882, after remaining almost two decades in Cordova, Onneca left to its Muslim children [13] and returned to Pamplona with its father, who had recently taken possession of the throne. Shortly after returning, she married hi
2 CONC s cousin Aznar Sánchez de Larraún, son of Sancho Garces and grandson of Garcia Iniguez of Pamplona
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NAVARRE.htm#AssonaIniguez
2 CONT
2 CONT *Íñigo "Arista" & his wife ONECA had four children:
2 CONT **1. GARCÍA Iñíguez ([810]-killed by Arabs [Lumberri] 882[57], bur Leire Monastery). The Codex de Roda names "Garsea Enneconis et domna Assona…et domna ---" m [firstly] URRACA, daughter of ---. García I & his [first] wife had [fou
2 CONC r] children:
2 CONT ***b) SANCHO García . The Codex de Roda names "Fortunio Garseanis et Sanzio Garseanis et domna Onneca" as the children of "Garsea Enneconis" and his unnamed wife[68]. m ---. The name of Sancho's wife is not known. Sancho García & 
2 CONC his wife had [two] children: …
2 CONT ****i) '''AZNAR Sánchez de Larraún''' . The Codex de Roda names "Asnari Sanziones qui et Larron" as son of "Sanzio Garseanis"[69]. m (880) [as her second husband,] his first cousin, ONECA [%C3%8D%C3%B1iga] Fortún de Pamplona, [rep
2 CONC udiated wife of ABD ALLAH later ABD ALLAH I Emir of Córdoba], … Aznar Sánchez & his wife had three children:
2 CONT ***** (a)       SANCHO Aznárez .  The Codex de Roda names "Santio Asnari et domna Tota regina et domna Sanzia" as the children of "Asnari Sanziones qui et Larron" and his wife[73]. 
2 CONT *****(b)       TODA Aznárez ([885]-after 970).  The Codex de Roda names "Santio Asnari et domna Tota regina et domna Sanzia" as the children of "Asnari Sanziones qui et Larron" and his wife, one manuscript specifying that Tota was
2 CONC  the wife of "Sanctii Obtimi regis"[74].  m SANCHO I García King of Navarre, son of GARCÍA II Jiménez King of Pamplona & his second wife Dadildis de Pallars ([880]-11 Dec 925, bur San Estebán).
2 CONT *****(c)       SANCHA Aznárez.  The Codex de Roda names "Santio Asnari et domna Tota regina et domna Sanzia" as the children of "Asnari Sanziones qui et Larron" and his wife, in a later passage naming "domna Sanzia, Asnari Santion
2 CONC is filia" as wife of "Scemeno Garseanis" and recording that she was killed "in Galias in villa…Laco" by her son García Jiménez[75].  m JIMENO García de Pamplona, son of GARCÍA II Jimenez King of Pamplona & his second wife Dadildis
2 CONC  de Pallars (-931). 
2 CONT **** ii)         [VELASQUITA Sánchez.  Al-Udri records that "Mutarrif ibn Musa" married "Faliskita, hija de Sanyo, señor de Pamplona" and that he brought her to Huesca (which suggests that the marriage should be dated to [870/71] 
2 CONC when Mutarif took control of Huesca) and had children by her[76].  The date of her marriage is consistent with Velasquita having been the daughter of Sancho, son of García I Iñíguez [King] of Pamplona, but this is not confirmed be
2 CONC yond all doubt by the passage in Al-Udri.  m ([871/72]) as his [---] wife, MUTARIF ibn Musa, son of MUSA Ibn Musa & his wife --- (-crucified Córdoba 6 Sep 873).] 
2 CONT ----
