2 CONT ABD al-RAHMAN ([792]-23 Sep 852).  Abd el-Wahid Merrakechi records "…Abd er-Rahman b. Hakam b. Hicham b. Mohammed b. Abd er-Rahman ed-Dakhil…" when reciting the ancestry of his descendant "El-Motadd billah" Emir of Córdoba[67].  H
2 CONC e succeeded his father 822 as ABD al-RAHMAN II Emir of Córdoba.  During his reign, the court became more formal, the administration of government more organised (following eastern Islamic models), and the respect of Islamic tradit
2 CONC ion imposed more strictly.  He also encouraged scholars and poets, and constructed mosques in Seville and Jaen, as well as an extension to the mosque in Córdoba.  He founded the city of Murcia in 831.  In Summer 844, Viking warshi
2 CONC ps attacked Seville, but the invaders were effectively beaten by the Emir's troops after they landed.  The Chronicon Albeldense records that “Abderahaman” reigned 32 years and six months in Córdoba while Ordoño I was king of Astur
2 CONC ias, adding in a later paragraph that he was the son of “Haccam”[68].  Abd al-Rahman II had five children:  
2 CONT
2 CONT # al-MUTARRIF
2 CONT # MUHAMMAD ([822]-Aug 886).  The Chronicon Albeldense names “Mahomat” as the son of “Abderrhaman”[69].  Abd el-Wahid Merrakechi records "…Mohammed b. Abd er-Rahman b. Hakam b. Hicham…" when reciting the ancestry of his descendant 
2 CONC "El-Motadd billah" Emir of Córdoba[70].  He was installed as Governor of Zaragoza after his father conquered it in 844.  He besieged León in 846[71].  He succeeded his father 852 as MUHAMMAD Emir of Córdoba.  He put down a rebelli
2 CONC on in 854 in Toledo, and in 868 in Merida.  Separatist movements also developed around Badajoz and Malaga.  Muhammad had six children.
2 CONT # al-MUNDHIR .  He attacked Álava in [849/50][77]
2 CONT # ABD ALLAH .  Son of Emir Abd al-Rahman's favourite concubine Turab
2 CONT # HISHAM 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Abd Al Rahman II De Córdoba (b. 792, d. 22 Sep 852)
2 CONT
2 CONT Abd Al Rahman II De Córdoba (son of Al Hakam I de Córdoba and Adjab) was born 792, and died 22 Sep 852. He married Al Shifa.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Notes for Abd Al Rahman II De Córdoba: BIOGRAPHY: Subiu ao trono com 20 anos.Foi muito genioso, cultivou a poesia e protegeu as artes e letras.
2 CONT
2 CONT Era alto, moreno, de olhos grandes e negros. Tinha larga barba.
2 CONT
2 CONT A sua corte foi considerada a mais brilhante da época, sob o seu re
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Abd Al Rahman II De Córdoba and Al Shifa are: +Mohammed De Córdoba, b. 823, d. 04 Aug 886.
