2 CONT '''Medlands'''
2 CONT
2 CONT al-HAKAM, son of HISHAM I Emir of Córdoba ([770/75]-822).  Abd el-Wahid Merrakechi records "…Hakam b. Hicham b. Mohammed b. Abd er-Rahman ed-Dakhil…" when reciting the ancestry of his descendant "El-Motadd billah" Emir of Córdoba[
2 CONC 63].  In an earlier passage, Abd el-Wahid Merrakechi names El-Hakam as son of Hisham and "une concubine…Zokhrouf", adding that he was about 22 years old when he succeeded his father and was "un homme impie et débauché"[64].  He su
2 CONC cceeded his father 796 as al-HAKAM I Emir of Córdoba.  Distracted by the challenges to the succession by his uncles Sulayman and Abd-Allah, attacks on the Christians decreased at the start of his reign.  However, by 810 the attack
2 CONC s intensified again and in 816 Emir al-Hakam launched a major offensive against the kingdom of Asturias[65].  The Chronicon Albeldense records that “Alhacam” reigned 26 years and six months in Córdoba, adding in a later paragraph 
2 CONC that he was the son of “Iscem”[66]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT al-Hakam had five children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT # ABD al-RAHMAN ([792]-23 Sep 852).  Abd el-Wahid Merrakechi records "…Abd er-Rahman b. Hakam b. Hicham b. Mohammed b. Abd er-Rahman ed-Dakhil…" when reciting the ancestry of his descendant "El-Motadd billah" Emir of Córdoba[67]. 
2 CONC  He succeeded his father 822 as ABD al-RAHMAN II Emir of Córdoba.  During his reign, the court became more formal, the administration of government more organised (following eastern Islamic models), and the respect of Islamic trad
2 CONC ition imposed more strictly.  He also encouraged scholars and poets, and constructed mosques in Seville and Jaen, as well as an extension to the mosque in Córdoba.  He founded the city of Murcia in 831.  In Summer 844, Viking wars
2 CONC hips attacked Seville, but the invaders were effectively beaten by the Emir's troops after they landed.  The Chronicon Albeldense records that “Abderahaman” reigned 32 years and six months in Córdoba while Ordoño I was king of Ast
2 CONC urias, adding in a later paragraph that he was the son of “Haccam”[68].  Abd al-Rahman II had five children.
2 CONT
2 CONT #  al-MUGHIRA
2 CONT #  SAID
2 CONT # UMAYYA
2 CONT # al-WALID bin al-HAKAM .  He led an army to attack Galicia in 838[78].   
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Al Hakam I de Córdoba (b. 770, d. 21 May 822)
2 CONT
2 CONT Al Hakam I de Córdoba (son of Hisham I de Córdoba) was born 770, and died 21 May 822. He married Adjab.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Notes for Al Hakam I de Córdoba: BIOGRAPHY: Subiu ao trono com 26 anos.
2 CONT
2 CONT De pele morena, alto e delgado, era cruel e impiedoso.
2 CONT
2 CONT Preocupou-se, todavia, com a cultura dos seus súbditos mandando construir diversas escolas. Mandou vir, para o efeito, professores do Oriente.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Al Hakam I de Córdoba and Adjab are: +Abd Al Rahman II De Córdoba, b. 792, d. 22 Sep 852.
