2 CONT (From Wikipedia) Sancho García (died 1017), called of the Good Laws (in Spanish, el de los Buenos Fueros), was the count of Castile and Álava from 995 to his death. He was the son of Count García Fernández, against whom he rebelle
2 CONC d with the support of Almanzor, the effective ruler of Córdoba. This resulted in the partition of the county between Sancho and his father, and the county was not reunited until his father's death five years later. He was succeede
2 CONC d by his own son García.
2 CONT
2 CONT His wife was named Urraca, whose origin has been subject to speculation. The current consensus makes her his cousin, the daughter of count Gómez Díaz of Saldaña, head of the Beni Gómez family, by Muniadona Fernández of Castile.
2 CONT
