1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT < [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fernando_Bermúdez_de_Cea Wikipedia] > '''Fernando Bermúdez''' (died c. 978), the second Count of Cea, was the son of Bermudo Núñez and his wife Argilo.[1][2][a] As the father of a queen of Navarre,
2 CONC  and therefore, ancestor of many royal houses, Fernando was a distinguished member of the highest ranks of the nobility of the Kingdom of León.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage and issue
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Elvira Díaz, daughter of Diego Muñoz, count of Saldaña, and his wife Tregidia.[7][b] They were the parents of:[8]
2 CONT
2 CONT # Pedro Fernández (died ca. 1028), the third Count of Cea and lacking a male heir, the agnate line of the counts of Cea was extinguished. With his wife, Sancha Muñoz, he had only one daughter named Elvira Pérez.[9]
2 CONT # Gómez Fernández (died before 978),[9] was the husband of Onecca and father of Countess Onecca Gómez, wife of Count Fortún who was most likely a member of the royal house of Pamplona. He was probably the father of Fernando and Ro
2 CONC drigo Gómez.[9][c]
2 CONT # Gotina Fernández, the wife of Count Pelayo Rodríguez.[11]
2 CONT # Jimena Fernández, Queen consort as the wife of King García Sánchez II and mother of King Sancho III of Navarre.[11]
2 CONT # Justa Fernández, the first wife of Count Flaín Muñoz.[11]
2 CONT # Elvira Fernández.[11]
