2 CONT * d)         ['''FERNANDO Muñoz''' (-1103 or after).  Mayordomo of Alfonso VI King of Castile from 20 Jan 1096 to 31 Jul 1101.  Salazar y Acha suggests that Fernando Muñoz may have been the son of Munio Rodríguez & his first wife[
2 CONC 861].  However, it appears that the position of mayordomo was held mainly by nobles at the beginning of their careers.  Assuming that the marriage date of Munio Rodríguez is correctly stated above, this would not be the case with 
2 CONC Fernando Muñoz if he was their son.  …  “...Fernando Monniz...” confirmed the charter dated 25 Jan 1100 under which King Alfonso VI donated “villa...Uillaverde...in Ualle de Uidriales...ex successione comitis Monnini Fernandiz, a 
2 CONC patria exilio propter superbiam suam religati” to Sahagún[865].  Conde en Astorga 1100.] 
