2 CONT D. Gomes Pais da Silva (1120 - ?) He was a Portuguese nobleman and knight of Afonso I of Portugal.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://pt.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gomes_Pais_da_Silva
2 CONT
2 CONT As a knight he participated in the battle of Ourique fought in 1139 and in the capture of Lisbon in 1147. He was lord of Torre de Silva, lord of Alderete, and lord of Porto da Figueira in 1170. He was the mayor of the Castle of Sa
2 CONC nta Eulália and Guimarães.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family relationships
2 CONT
2 CONT He was D's son. Paio Guterres da Silva (1070 — 1129) and D. Sancha Anes (1080 — ?), daughter of Juan Ramirez, Lord of Montoro. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married D. Urraca Nunes Velho (1130 — ?), daughter of Nuno Soares Velho and Môr Pires Perna, from whom she had:
2 CONT
2 CONT * D. Paio Gomes da Silva (1170 — ?) Married to D. Maria Fernandes
2 CONT * D. Martim Gomes da Silva (1150 - ?) Married to Urraca Rodrigues, daughter of Rodrigo Fernandes de Toronho and Aldonça Peres.
2 CONT * D. Maria Gomes da Silva married to Paio Soares Correia.
2 CONT * D. Urraca Gomes da Silva (1160 — ?) Married to Gomes Mendes de Briteiros.
