2 CONT 2907 / 5000 Translation results D. Fernando Mendes «the Old Man»
2 CONT
2 CONT Senhor de Bragança (1st) (Ferdinandus Menendez de Braganções) image Rich-Man Born circa 1030 Deceased circa August 1117 At the age of possibly 87 years Parents
2 CONT
2 CONT D. Mendo Alaniz Ne Artsrouni Marriages and children
2 CONT
2 CONT Married to Ne Alfonso de Castilla ca 1058, they had D. Mendo Fernandes ca 1073-ca 1139 Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT In a document dated 25.8.1072 he is referred to as "princeps ipsus terre" of Chaves. The 1.3.1112 confirms a document from Count D. Henrique. In 1113 he was governor of Vila Lobos. In August 1117, the year in which he will have di
2 CONC ed, he was governor of Toro and Zamora. In 1055 he freed the lands at the source of the Távora river from the Moors, which he took out of presumption. He refounded Braganções (later Bragança), on the old Roman Brigantia. He docume
2 CONC nts himself as governor of Chaves by D. Afonso VI, whose daughter (certainly a bastard) he seems to have married, according to Livro Velho.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT
2 CONT Manuel Abranches de Soveral ------------------------------------------------- ---
2 CONT
2 CONT 2nd D. Fernando Mendes de Bragança, rich man, called the Elder; he succeeded his father in the lordship of Bragança, and more lands, which were many in the province of Trás-os-Montes, between Bragança and Miranda. The old book say
2 CONC s, which was in the Tombo tower, and shows the chronicler Brandão, p. 3rd liv. 10th chap. 4th of the Lusitanian Monarchy, and book 8th chap. 27, who had been married to a daughter of King Affonso VI of Leon,
2 CONT
