2 CONT ----------
2 CONT
2 CONT Roger II (22 December 1095[1] – 26 February 1154) was King of Sicily, son of Roger I of Sicily and successor to his brother Simon. He began his rule as Count of Sicily in 1105, later became Duke of Apulia and Calabria (1127), then
2 CONC  King of Sicily (1130). It is Roger II's distinction to have united all the Norman conquests in Italy into one kingdom with a strong centralized government.
2 CONT
2 CONT Contents
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 Background 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 Reign 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.1 Rise to power in Sicily 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.2 Rise to power in southern Italy 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.2.1 Royal investiture 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.2.2 Peninsular rebellions 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.2.3 Imperial invasion 
2 CONT
