2 CONT Tributacion de un palacio con sus heredamientos en Asieso.
2 CONT Fecha Creacion:
2 CONT 1318-02-04, (Santa Cruz de la Seros) -
2 CONT Toda Perez de San Vicente, abadesa del monasterio, da a Martin de Ayes, a su mujer Sancha, a Bernardo de Guazer y a su mujer Tomasa un palacio con sus heredamientos situado en Asieso por el pago anual de 5 potos y medio y una libr
2 CONC a de aceite.
2 CONT Lengua/Escritura de la Documentacion:
2 CONT Castellano
2 CONT Indices de Descripcion:
2 CONT Benedictinas
2 CONT Monasterio de Santa Maria de Santa Cruz de la Seros (Huesca)
2 CONT Santa Cruz de la Seros (Huesca)
2 CONT Historical records show that a lot of French Templiers immigrated to Spain to take up the fight against the Moors. Contracts were made between the rulers of Aragon, etc with the Templiers. The contract was simple, for every town c
2 CONC onquered by the templiers they would get a huge grant of the land and in some cases, castles and palaces.
2 CONT I am theorizing that the Ayes heritage began in France, see map of Asieso, France and the Alps are very close making immigration very easy by horseback. 
2 CONT My mother's DNA speaks to me of Haplo Group C, but embedded within her sequences are those of the French which were passed to her by her father, Feliciano Ayes y Ortiz. The sequences in essence, connect me to my French Ayes.
2 CONT The Surname, Aix doesn't roll off the Spanish tongue too well and one can see how the surname Aix would have been transcribed to become Ayes. Even Puerto Ricans had trouble with my 5th great grandfather's surname, Ales, that event
2 CONC ually transposed to Ayez and then to Ayes. History repeats itself.
2 CONT Update: 06/23/2008 via Betty Hubbard via yDNA Project Forum.
2 CONT Betty Hubbard - Jun 20, 2008
2 CONT "Toda Perez is Gutierre Clan-PEREZ DE TRABA, sister of Trastamara Count Fernando Perez de Traba, their father Count of Trastamara Pedro Froilaz.   Go to History file name GUTIERRE CLAN pg 1 -H. Gutierrez- browse -Count of Trastama
2 CONC ra Pedro Froilaz.   I was excited to find the surname AYES in your search of AYES surname connecting to PEREZ DE TRABA!   This AYES has to be related to PEREZ DE TRABA because only close kins they favor give lands to each other du
2 CONC ring these times.   I also remembered my grandfather giving lands to his kins before I was born but during his time lands were cheap; lands had gone up in value in the Phil these days.   I was surprised to hear last month that the
2 CONC  house of my grandfather was sold to someone, when I asked who sold it, it was sold by my distant aunt. "
2 CONT Research Copyright 2008, John J. Browne Ayes
