2 CONT History: Ferdinand II (of León) (1137-88), king of León (1157-88). He was the second son of Alfonso II, king of Castile, who was also king of León as Alfonso VII. Ferdinand was noted both for his intermittent wars with Castile and
2 CONC  Portugal and for his reorganization, about 1170, of the military Order of Saint James of the Sword (Santiago de la Espada) to participate in the campaign to drive the Moors from Spain.
2 CONT
