2 CONC  he was succeeded by his son, Roger III. The death of Roger III. about 1149, and of his son, Roger Bernard I., in 1188,. brought the county to Roger Bernard's only son, Raymond Roger, who, in 1190, accompanied the French king, Phi
2 CONC lip Augustus, to Palestine and distinguished himself at the capture of Acre.
