2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT   (Redirected from Berenguer Ramon I, Count of Provence)
2 CONT
2 CONT Berengar Raymond I (Catalan: Berenguer Ramon) (1115 – 1144) was the count of Provence (1131-1144). The younger son of Raymond Berengar III, count of Barcelona, and Douce of Provence. While his older brother Raymond Berengar receiv
2 CONC ed Barcelona (his father's inheritance), he received Provence (his mother's).
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Beatrice, heiress of Melgueil. His reign was occupied in wars with the family of Baux, which claimed the throne. He also took an offensive against Genoa, but died at Melgueil. His son Raymond Berengar succeeded him in P
2 CONC rovence, but Melgueil went to Beatrice' second husband, Bernard V Pelet.
