2 CONT
2 CONT TANCRED di Lecce, illegitimate son of ROGER of Sicily Duke of Apulia & his mistress --- di Lecce ([Lecce 1138]-Palermo 20 Feb 1194).  Hugo Falcandus records that "Tancred and William, the sons of Duke Roger by a nobly born mother…
2 CONC were kept under arrest within the palace compound" after the conspiracy against Guillaume I King of Sicily in [1156][606].  The Ryccardus de Sancti Germano Chronica name "Tancredus…ducis Roggerii filius…naturalis" but do not name 
2 CONC his mother[607].  Hugo Falcandus names "the duke's son Tancred" among those responsible for the capture of Guillaume I King of Sicily in 1161[608].  The "Catalogus Baronum", dated to [1166/68], records "terra comitis Tancredi fili
2 CONC i domini ducis Rogerii" holding fees previously held by "comitis Goffridi Montis Caveosi, sicut dixit idem comes Goffridus" in the county of Lecce, with "feudum militum XX et cum augmento milites XL"[609].  William of Tyre (Contin
2 CONC uator) names him "cosin germain" of Guillaume II King of Sicily when recording his accession in 1190[610].  He was exiled for involvement in a plot against King Guillaume I in 1161, but pardoned by Queen Margarita.  The Chronicle 
2 CONC of Romualdo Guarna records that "comes Guilielmus de Principatu et Riccardus de Mandra et Alexander monachus" were released from prison during a rebellion, dated to [1160] from the context, adding that "Guilielmus comes de Princip
2 CONC atu et Tancredus comes de Lycia" joined "ad Matthæum Bonellam"[611].  He was invested as Conte di Lecce in 1169.  He was appointed "Great Constable and Master Justiciar of the whole of Apulia and Terra di Lavoro" by King Guillaume
2 CONC  II.  He led the Sicilian fleet which arrived at Alexandria 25 Jul 1174 but sailed away within a week for lack of support from Byzantium or Jerusalem[612].  The Annales Casenses record that in 1176 "comes Roggerius et comes Tancre
2 CONC dus" went to Andria[613].  The Annales Ceccanenses record that in 1185 Guillaume King of Sicily appointed "comitem Tancredum" as captain of his fleet[614].  He was unlawfully elected as TANCRED King of Sicily in 1190 by the States
2 CONC  General of Sicily, called by Matteo d'Aiello [Vice-chancellor of Sicily], because of unease at the prospect of personal union of the crowns of Sicily and Germany if Tancred's aunt Constance succeeded as queen.  He was crowned at 
2 CONC Palermo 18 Jan 1190, and was finally recognised as king by the Pope under the Treaty of Gravina in 1192.  After his election, King Tancred kept his predecessor's Queen Joan in confinement.[615].  After her release was demanded by 
2 CONC her brother Richard I King of England (who was travelling through Italy on his way to join the Third Crusade in Palestine), she was sent to join him at Messina but the English king captured Messina to force Tancred to negotiate te
2 CONC rms over the inheritance of King Guillaume.  The treaty signed included the betrothal of Tancred's daughter to Richard's nephew Arthur de Bretagne[616].  Heinrich VI King of Germany was marching on Naples and Sicily to enforce his
2 CONC  rights, when Tancred died.  The Annales Casenses record the death in 1194 of "rex Tancredus" at "Panormum"[617].  The Annales Siculi record the death 20 Feb 1194 of "rex Tancredus"[618].  The monk Conrad´s Brevis Chronica records
2 CONC  the death 20 Feb 1194 of "Rex Tancredus"[619]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' SIBILLA, daughter of [RINALDO [I] d’Aquino & his second wife ---] ([before 1165]-after 1195).  ... ... .... ....
2 CONT
