1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SPANISH%20NOBILITY%20LATER%20MEDIEVAL.htm#GonzaloMaranondied1178
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         [GONZALO [Rodríguez] de Marañón (-after 21 Nov 1178).  Salazar y Castro records his parentage[1984].  Martínez Díez states that he was unable to confirm this supposed affiliation in documentation[1985].  His patronymic 
2 CONC "Rodríguez" is confirmed by the charter dated 27 May 1182 under which "domina Maria filia comitis Amalrici" donated "casas…in Burgis…in barrio Sancti Romani" to Burgos Cathedral, witnessed by "Petrus Gonsaluez filius Gonsaluo Rois
2 CONC  dus…"[1986], assuming that the son can be identified as the son of Gonzalo de Marañón as appears likely.  Alférez of Alfonso VII King of Castile 7 Feb 1155 to 30 Jul 1157.  "…Gundisaluus de Maranon alferiz imperatoris…" subscribe
2 CONC d the charter dated 7 Feb 1155 under which King Alfonso VII donated property near Lédigos to Santiago de Compostela[1987].  "Aldefonsus…tocius Hyspanie imperator…cum uxore mea imperatrice domna Rica et…filiis meis Sanctio et Ferra
2 CONC ndo regibus" donated property to the abbey of Silos by charter dated 28 Oct 1155, confirmed by "…Gundisalvus de Maranon alferiz imperatoris…"[1988].  "Martinus Fernandez" sold various properties to "Gundisalvo Ferrandiz fratri meo
2 CONC " by charter dated 1156, the dating clause of which names "…Gunzaluo Maranon alfieraz inperatoris…"[1989].  Alfonso VIII King of Castile granted "la villa de Sequilla, sita en el río de Francos…en el término de Cobos de Cerrato" t
2 CONC o Gonzalo and his wife by charter dated 1 Mar 1169[1990].  Conde 9 Jan 1174[1991].]  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' MAYOR García, daughter of GARCÍA García Señor de Aza & his [first wife --- de Lara] (-after 24 May 1182).  Salazar y Castro records her marriage[1992].  Alfonso VIII King of Castile granted "la villa de Sequilla, sita en e
2 CONC l río de Francos…en el término de Cobos de Cerrato" to Gonzalo and his wife by charter dated 1 Mar 1169[1993].  A charter dated Jan 1182 records the entry of her daughter Inés in the Cistercian monastery of Aza, in the presence of
2 CONC  her mother "Mayor García", subscribed by her children "Fernando, Pedro, Alberico, Nuño, Domicio, Inés"[1994].  "Cometissa domina Maior" donated "hereditatem de albegeria de Oterdaios et de Paramo et de Villaymara" to Burgos Cathe
2 CONC dral by charter dated 26 May 1182[1995] (which follows an earlier donation to Burgos dated 1159 by her supposed father: "Garcia Garciez filius comite Garcie…cum uxore mea Sancia" donated part of "albergeria de Oterdaios sicut mate
2 CONC r mea et fratres mei dederunt" to Burgos Cathedral by charter dated Dec 1159[1996]).  
2 CONT
2 CONT  Gonzalo & his wife had six children: 
