1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/CATALAN%20NOBILITY.htm#HugoIIIAmpurias
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         HUG [III] de Empúries (-[20 Apr 1173/25 May 1174]).  He succeeded his father as Comte de Empúries.  “Hugo Impuritanensis comes...cum comitissis Brunissendis...matre mea et Jusiane uxore mea et filio nostro Poncio et Pon
2 CONC cio fratre meo” donated the serf “Castilionem filium Petri Juliani” to Santa Maria de Roses by charter dated 7 Dec 1167[1574].  "Ugo…comes Impuriarum" donated property to the monastery of Poblet by charter dated 11 Nov 1170, subsc
2 CONC ribed by "Iosiane comitisse, Poncii filii eorum"[1575].  “Brunisendis comitissa” donated “mansum...in parroechia Sancti Iuliani de Virginibus quem inhabitat Guililemus Firma Colades” to Sant Daniel de Girona, for the soul of “viri
2 CONC  mei Poncii Ugonis comitis”, with the advice of “filii mei Poncii”, by charter dated 20 Apr 1173, signed by “Brunisendis comitisse, Poncii filii eius, Iusiane comitissa, Poncii filii eius”[1576].  The Chronicon alterum Rivipullens
2 CONC e records 1173 “Ugo Impuriensis comes, et --- comes Rusilionis”, without specifying that this was the year of their deaths[1577].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' JUSIANA de Entenza Señora de Alcolea, daughter of BERNAT de Entenza Señor de Alcolea & his wife Gersenda de Pallars (-after 1192).  “Hugo Impuritanensis comes...cum comitissis Brunissendis...matre mea et Jusiane uxore mea 
2 CONC et filio nostro Poncio et Poncio fratre meo” donated the serf “Castilionem filium Petri Juliani” to Santa Maria de Roses by charter dated 7 Dec 1167[1578].  "Ugo…comes Impuriarum" donated property to the monastery of Poblet by cha
2 CONC rter dated 11 Nov 1170, subscribed by "Iosiane comitisse, Poncii filii eorum"[1579].  “Brunisendis comitissa” donated “mansum...in parroechia Sancti Iuliani de Virginibus quem inhabitat Guililemus Firma Colades” to Sant Daniel de 
2 CONC Girona, for the soul of “viri mei Poncii Ugonis comitis”, with the advice of “filii mei Poncii”, by charter dated 20 Apr 1173, signed by “Brunisendis comitisse, Poncii filii eius, Iusiane comitissa, Poncii filii eius”[1580].  "Pon
2 CONC cius Ugonis comes Impuritanensis et mater mea Iusiana" donated property to the monastery of Poblet, for the soul of "patris mei Ugonis", by charter dated 25 May 1174[1581].  “Poncius Ugonis Impuriarum comes cum matre mea Jusiana” 
2 CONC donated “mansum de ipsa Rocha que inhabitat Petrus Eschazer” to Santa Maria de Roses, for the soul of “Ugonis fratris meo defuncti”, by charter dated 21 Sep 1174[1582].  “Poncius Ugonis...Impuriarum comes” confirmed navigation rig
2 CONC hts from cap de Creus to La Muga for Santa Maria de Roses by charter dated 26 Jan 1184, signed by “Jusiane matris eius...”[1583].  Hugo [III] & his wife had three children: 
