2 CONT Vv. 96-98. And, in search of Raquel and Vidas, Martín Antolínez crosses the river, passes through the arch of Santa María and through La Llana; and, not finding them, he crosses Fernán González Street and part of San Esteban Stree
2 CONC t, and goes up the path that crossed old Burgos to reach the Castle and there he found them. It is the path that Martín Antolínez, alone or accompanied by Raquel and Vidas, walks and retraces until he obtains the loan that El Cid 
2 CONC needed. Once the money was obtained, El Cid set up camp and headed for San Pedro de Cardeña along Calle de la Calera and Calle de Cortes while Martín Antolínez said goodbye to his wife in Burgos.
