1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SPANISH%20NOBILITY%20LATER%20MEDIEVAL.htm#NunoGonzalezLaradied1291
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.     '''    NUÑO González de Lara''' (-Lisbon 1291).  The Nobiliario of Pedro Conde de Barcelos names "D. Juan Nuñez el Gordo, D. Nuño Gonçalez, que murio en Lisboa" as the children of "D. Nuño Gonçalez de Lara" and his wife "D.
2 CONC  Teresa Alonso"[1714].  Salazar y Castro records his parentage[1715].  The Crónica del Rey Don Alfonso X records disputes between the king and "nuño Gonzalez, fijo de don Nuño…don Nuño su padre e a don Juan Nuñez su hermano"[1716]
2 CONC .  The testament of "Nuño Gonzalez", dated 15 Jan 1286, appoints as his heir "doña Joanna Gomez mi muger” and “si...no ovies fijos de mi...a fijos de don Joan mi hermano"[1717].  Salazar y Castro quotes the charter of King Sancho 
2 CONC dated 29 Oct 1288, confirming the privileges of the monastery of San Salvador de Sotillo de Haccam, witnessed by “D. Juan Nuñez, D. Nuño Gonzalvez...D. Johan fijo de D. Johan Nuñez, D. Nuño Gonzalez so hermano”[1718].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' JUANA Gómez Girón, daughter of GÓMEZ González Girón & his wife Aldara Añez de Sossa.  The Livro Velho names "Joanna Gomes molher de D. Nuno de Lara" as the child of "D. Gomes Gonçalues Giron" and his wife[1719].  The Nobil
2 CONC iario of Pedro Conde de Barcelos names "D. Juana Gomez" as the child of "D. Gomes Gonçalez Giron" and his wife "Doña Aldara Anez", recording in an earlier passage that "D. Nuño Gonçalez de Lara" married "D. Juana Gomez" and that t
2 CONC he couple was childless[1720].  The testament of "Nuño Gonzalez", dated 15 Jan 1286, names "doña Joanna Gomez mi muger…don Joan mi hermano"[1721]. 
