2 CONC  of Baudouin Count of Flanders who was considered a less powerful candidate.  Her second husband installed her as regent of Thessaloniki while he was on campaign to conquer Thessaly[794].  She was also regent for her infant son af
2 CONC ter the death of her husband, but in the face of opposition from local nobles was replaced by Uberto di Biandrate.  The primary source which confirms her third marriage has not so far been identified.  She was restored as regent b
