1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mayor Guillén de Guzmán ( ?, 1205 - Alcocer ,1262 ).
2 CONT
2 CONT Born into one of the level two "richmen" families of King Ferdinand III's court, she was the daughter of Guillén Pérez de Guzmán, and sister of Pedro de Guzmán, Castile's first adelantado and father of Alonso Pérez de Guzmán.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was mentioned in chronicles and documents of the time mainly for being the lover of prince Alfonso de Castilla, future king Alfonso X of Castile, son of Ferdinand III of Castile and Beatriz de Suabia.
2 CONT
2 CONT From her relation with prince Alfonso she had three children[citation needed]:
2 CONT
2 CONT *Beatrice (1242 - 1303), married to Alfonso III of Portugal and mother of Denis I of Portugal;
2 CONT *Martín Alfonso de Castilla (? - ?), abbot in Valladolid
2 CONT * Urraca (? - ?).
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on 4 October 1262. Her body was buried in the monastery of the Order of Poor Ladies of San Miguel del Monte. After moving to Alcocer, her body was moved as well, and it curiously remained intact until the beginning othe 2
2 CONC 1st century. In 1936, it disapeared together with a polycromated wooden statue, considered among he best funerary art from the Middle Ages in Guadalajara[citation needed].
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mayor_Guillen_de_Guzm%C3%A1n
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Beatrice of Castile (1242-1303)
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Beatrice of Castile was an illegitimate daughter of Alfonso X of Castile and Maria de Guzman.
2 CONT
