0 @N6000000000437119799@ NOTE Name Prefix:<NPFX> King Name Suffix:<NSFX> Vi, Of Castile And Leon "The Valiant" born before June 1040 died 1109, Toledo, Castile King of León (1065–70) and of Castile and León (1072–1109). known as Alfonso the Brave He inherited 
1 CONC León from his father, Ferdinand I, and warred with his envious brother Sancho II.On Sancho's death he inherited Castile (1072); he also occupied Galicia and imprisoned his brother García, its rightful ruler. In 1077 Alfonso procla
1 CONC imed himself emperor of all Spain. He took Toledo from the Muslims, but his demands fortribute led to the invasion of Spain by the North African Almoravids, and he was defeated at Zallaqah (1086). The Cid became an ally and defend
1 CONC ed eastern Spain, but Alfonso continued to lose ground against the Berber armies.
