0 @N6000000000337427812@ NOTE Weis, p. 159 - Count de Toulouse
0 @N6000000000437137736@ NOTE Name Prefix:<NPFX> Count Name Suffix:<NSFX> Of Toulouse And Albi
0 @N6000000000945065468@ NOTE Greve av Toulouse 1037 -  1060. 
1 CONT Pons var greve av Toulouse, Quercy, Albigeois og herre over Auvergne. Gjennom sin
1 CONT mor, Emma, hadde han rett til grevskapet Avignon. Han antar senere titelen ?compte palatin?.
1 CONT Han ble ekskommunisert for å ha forstøtt sin hustru og ektet en annen.
1 CONT I 1053 grunnlegger han klosteret Vigan og forener klosteret Psalmodie med Moissac i
1 CONT Cluny og S. Victor i Marseille.
1 CONT Pons ble gift ca. 1037 med Majore, vistnok av huset Carcasona eller Foix. Hun døde
1 CONT antagelig få år senere. Majore var antagelig hans andre eller tredje hustru.
1 CONT Han giftet seg så med Almodis ca. 1040-45, men forstøtte henne ca. 1053-54.
1 CONT Han levde enda i 1060, da han var tilstede ved et møte i Toulouse. Pons døde senest i
1 CONT begynnelsen av 1061 og er begravet i St. Sernin i Toulouse.
0 @N6000000001783162962@ NOTE Basic Life Information
1 CONT
1 CONT Pons of Toulouse
1 CONT
1 CONT Pons (II) William (abt 1020 - 1060) was the Count of Toulouse from 1037. He was the eldest son and successor of William III Taillefer and Emma of Provence. He thus inherited the title marchio Provincae. He is known to have owned m
1 CONC any allods and he relied on Roman, Salic, and Gothic law.
1 CONT
1 CONT Already in 1030, he possessed a lot of power in the Albigeois. In 1037, he gave many allodial churches and castles, including one half of that of Porta Spina, in the Albigeois, Nimois, and Provence as a bridal gift to his wife Maj
1 CONC ore.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1038, he split the purchase of the Diocese of Albi with the Trencavel family. In 1040, he donated property in Diens to Cluny. In 1047, he first appears as count palatine in a charter donating Moissac to Cluny.
1 CONT
1 CONT Pons married first wife, Majore, in 1022. She died in 1044. In 1045, he married, Almodis de La Marche, former wife of Hugh V of Lusignan, but he too repudiated her in 1053. His only child by Majore, Pons the Younger, did not inher
1 CONC it his county and march. His eldest sons by Almodis, William IV and Raymond IV, originally just count of Saint-Gilles, succeeded him in turn. His son Hugh became abbot of Saint-Gilles. He had one daughter, Almodis, who married the
1 CONC  count of Melgueil.
1 CONT
1 CONT Pons died in Toulouse and was buried in Saint-Sernin, probably late in 1060 or early in 1061.
1 CONT
1 CONT <http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pons_of_Toulouse>
