1 CONT PLAC Acceded: 1157
1 CONT Ferdinand inherited Leon in the division of his fathers kingdom. He ru led from 1157, until his death in 1188.  Ferdinand II (b. 1137 in Tole do, Castile, d. January 22, 1188) was the son of Alfonso VII of Castil e and León and of
1 CONC  Berenguela, of the House of Barcelona, and king of L eón from 1157 to his death. His father divided his kingdom upon his de ath, with Ferdinand receiving León and Sancho Castile.  His reign of t hirty years was one of strife mark
1 CONC ed by no signal success or reverse.H e had to contend with his unruly nobles, several of whom he put to dea th. During the minority of his nephew, Alfonso VIII of Castile, he end eavoured to impose himself on the kingdom as regent
1 CONC . On the west he wa s in more or less constant strife with the Kingdom of Portugal, which had separated from León in 1139. His relations to the Portuguese Hous e of Burgundy must have suffered by his repudiation of his wife Urraca
1 CONC  , daughter of King Afonso I of Portugal. Though he took the King of Po rtugal prisoner in 1169, he made no political use of his success. Heex tended his dominions southward in Extremadura at the expense of theMoo rs. Ferdinand, w
1 CONC ho died in 1188, left the reputation of a good knight and hard fighter, but did not display political or organising faculty . He was succeeded by his only son, Alfonso IX.
0 @N6000000002176683069@ NOTE He was the 2nd son of Alfonso II, King of Castile, who was also King of Leon
1 CONT as Alfonso VII. Ferdinand was noted both for his intermittent wars with
1 CONT Castile and Portugal, and for his reorgannization (c1170) of the military
1 CONT order of Saint James of the Sword to drive the Moors from Spain.
0 @N6000000002188182884@ NOTE Wa'il ibn Umayyah
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Wa'il ibn Umayya, also known as Abu al-As [citation needed] was the son of Umayya ibn Abd Shams.
1 CONT
1 CONT As his sons are mentioned:
1 CONT
1 CONT     * A'as ibn Wa'il, father of Amr ibn al-A'as[citation needed]
1 CONT     * Affan ibn Wa'il, father of Uthman[citation needed]
1 CONT     * Abu al-Hakim ibn Wa'il[citation needed]
1 CONT
1 CONT Another source also mentions:
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Hakam ibn Wa'il, also known as "al-Hakam ibn Abi al-`As" [1] aka "Hakam Ibn Abi al-As Ibn Umayya" [2][citation needed]
1 CONT
1 CONT He also had a daughter:
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Saffya binte abi al-A'as, who bore a daughter to Abu Safyan.
