1 CONT Alfonso II (Aragon) or Alfons I (Provence and Barcelona) (1152 - 1196), called the Chaste or the Troubadour, was the King of Aragon and Count of Barcelona from 1162 until his death. He was the son of Ramon Berenguer IV of Barcelon
