0 @N6000000002322298025@ NOTE The last Norman king of Sicily, under regency from 1166, he ruled in person
1 CONT from 1171. He became known as William the Good because of his clemency and
1 CONT justice towards the towns and the barons, in contrast with his father, William
1 CONT I the Bad. William's marriage was childless and he died while planning to
1 CONT join the Third Crusade.
