0 @N6000000003658751244@ NOTE From Plantagenet Ancestry:
1 CONT
1 CONT ... a mistress, Alice of France, daughter of Louis VII le Jeune (or le Pieux), King of France, by his 2nd wife, Constance, daughter of Alfonso VII, King of Castile and León.  Alice was born 4 Oct. 1160.  She was contracted to marr
1 CONC y King Henry II's son, Richard (afterwards King of England) in Jan. 1169.  King Richard voided his marriage contract with her at Messina in March 1190/1, after which she was restored to her brother King Philippe Auguste or France,
1 CONC  in 1195.  Alice subsequently married at Meudon 20 August 1196 Guillaume II Talvas. ... He was born say 1171 (adult by 1195).  She was living 28 July 1218.  By her legitimate daughter and heiress, Marie, Countes of Ponthieu and Mo
1 CONC ntreuil, Alice was great-grandmother of Eleanor of Castile, 1st wife of King Edward I of England.
0 @N6000000005598932889@ NOTE Some source indicate that Alice may have been the daughter of Louis an d his third wife Alix de Champagne (?).  Alice, was marked as the futu re wife of Richard then prince of England in 1169 and since that time had been associate
1 CONC d with the household of Henry II.  After 8 July 1174 , she was resident at the Castle of Devizes in Wiltshire.  She and he r proposed marriage to Richard were part of the discussions between Ri chard, her father Louis VII and Henr
1 CONC y II at Nanacourt in June of 1177 .  She was living with Henry II, Richards father while Eleanor of Aqui taine was held at Winchester or Sarum Castle in Salisbury.  When 'the young King' Henry died in 1183, the Norman Vexin passed
1 CONC  to Alice who h ad previously (1169) been betrothed to Richard, then Duc de Normandie .  Richard never showed any interest in the marriage.  After Richard a ssended to the reign of England, his mother Eleanor had Alice imprison ed
1 CONC  at Winchester.  By November of 1191, Alice was a prisoner at Rouen .  Sometime in mid 1195, Richard I gave in to Phillippes demands and s he was released from confinement at Rouen.  Phillippe soon had her mar ried to Guillaume II
1 CONC I - Count of Ponthieu.  After her marriage she spe nt the rest of her life in obsecurity.
