0 @N6000000002187834288@ NOTE Irene Angelina
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Irene Angelina (1177/1181 - 1208) was the daughter of the Byzantine emperor Isaac II Angelos by his first wife Herina.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1193 she married Roger III of Sicily, but he died on 24 December 1193. Irene was captured in the German invasion of Sicily , on 29 December 1194, and was married on 25 May 1197 to Philip of Swabia.
1 CONT
1 CONT Her father, who had been deposed in 1195, urged her to get Philip's support for his reinstatement; her brother, Alexius, subsequently spent some time at Philip's court during the preparations for the Fourth Crusade. She thus had a
1 CONC n early influence on the eventual diversion of the Crusade to Constantinople in 1204.
1 CONT
1 CONT She was described by Walther von der Vogelweide as "the rose without a thorn, the dove without guile."
1 CONT
1 CONT Philip and Irene had four daughters:
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Beatrice of Hohenstaufen (1198-1212), married Otto IV, Holy Roman Emperor
1 CONT     * Cunigunde of Hohenstaufen (1200-1248), married King Wenceslaus I, King of Bohemia
1 CONT     * Mary of Hohenstaufen (1201-1235), married Henry II, Duke of Brabant
1 CONT     * Elizabeth of Hohenstaufen (1203-1235), married King Ferdinand III of Castile
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Sources
1 CONT
1 CONT     * O city of Byzantium: annals of Niketas Choniates tr. Harry J. Magoulias (Detroit: Wayne State University Press, 1984).
